609 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 394 0 R
/T (In this study we adopted rearing and artificial infection method to obtain the healthy and five diseased silkworms, including nuclear polyhedrosis virues \(NPV\), nosemabombycis, beauveriabassiana, bacterial disease, and pesticide poisoning in same growth stage. Images were collected by using mobile phone and a disease dataset was constructed in actual condition. An improved Effecientnet algorithm was proposed to recognize image of the healthy and diseased silkworms. The average accuracy reached 94.37%. Hence, the above researches indicated that deep learning could accurately recognize silkworm diseases by using method of image recognition. )
/E (In this study we adopted rearing and artificial infection method to obtain the healthy and five diseased silkworms, including nuclear polyhedrosis virues \(NPV\), nosemabombycis, beauveriabassiana, bacterial disease, and pesticide poisoning in same growth stage. Images were collected by using mobile phone and a disease dataset was constructed in actual condition. An improved Effecientnet algorithm was proposed to recognize image of the healthy and diseased silkworms. The average accuracy reached 94.37%. Hence, the above researches indicated that deep learning could accurately recognize silkworm diseases by using method of image recognition. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
610 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 394 0 R
/T (In sericulture, silkworm diseases pose a significant threat to silk production, leading to substantial economic losses and reduced yield quality for farmers. Traditional disease detection methods rely heavily on manual inspection, which is time-consuming, labor- intensive, and prone to human error, especially in early stages of infection when visual symptoms may be subtle. Moreover, the lack of timely diagnosis often results in the rapid spread of infections, severely impacting the health of silkworms and overall productivity. To address these challenges, there is a pressing need for an automated, accurate, and real- time disease detection system that can assist farmers in identifying infections at an early stage. Leveraging advances in artificial intelligence and deep learning, particularly convolutional neural networks, can revolutionize disease monitoring in sericulture by providing efficient and reliable diagnostics directly from silkworm images. )
/E (In sericulture, silkworm diseases pose a significant threat to silk production, leading to substantial economic losses and reduced yield quality for farmers. Traditional disease detection methods rely heavily on manual inspection, which is time-consuming, labor- intensive, and prone to human error, especially in early stages of infection when visual symptoms may be subtle. Moreover, the lack of timely diagnosis often results in the rapid spread of infections, severely impacting the health of silkworms and overall productivity. To address these challenges, there is a pressing need for an automated, accurate, and real- time disease detection system that can assist farmers in identifying infections at an early stage. Leveraging advances in artificial intelligence and deep learning, particularly convolutional neural networks, can revolutionize disease monitoring in sericulture by providing efficient and reliable diagnostics directly from silkworm images. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
