/T (silkworm images forms the basis of this research. The study applies machine learning techniques, using the Histogram Oriented Gradient \(HOG\) feature descriptor combined with Kernel Principal Component Analysis \(KPCA\) and supervised classifiers. The integration of Support Vector Machines \(SVM\) with HOG and KPCA achieved high accuracy \(93.16%\), recall \(93.38%\), and precision \(91.94%\), offering a faster, more accurate alternative to manual detection methods. This approach holds great potential for developing real-time, IoT-based diagnostic tools that enable farmers to quickly identify infected silkworms, reducing disease spread and economic losses. )
/E (silkworm images forms the basis of this research. The study applies machine learning techniques, using the Histogram Oriented Gradient \(HOG\) feature descriptor combined with Kernel Principal Component Analysis \(KPCA\) and supervised classifiers. The integration of Support Vector Machines \(SVM\) with HOG and KPCA achieved high accuracy \(93.16%\), recall \(93.38%\), and precision \(91.94%\), offering a faster, more accurate alternative to manual detection methods. This approach holds great potential for developing real-time, IoT-based diagnostic tools that enable farmers to quickly identify infected silkworms, reducing disease spread and economic losses. )
