/T (Monitoring silkworm health is crucial for successful sericulture practices. This study integrates Internet of Things \(IoT\) devices with deep learning models to continuously monitor silkworm health parameters. Sensors collect data on temperature, humidity, and silkworm activity, which are analyzed using deep learning algorithms to detect early signs of stress or disease. The system provides real-time alerts to farmers, facilitating prompt interventions and reducing potential losses. )
/E (Monitoring silkworm health is crucial for successful sericulture practices. This study integrates Internet of Things \(IoT\) devices with deep learning models to continuously monitor silkworm health parameters. Sensors collect data on temperature, humidity, and silkworm activity, which are analyzed using deep learning algorithms to detect early signs of stress or disease. The system provides real-time alerts to farmers, facilitating prompt interventions and reducing potential losses. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
781 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 402 0 R
/T (This research explores the application of transfer learning techniques to classify diseases in silkworms. By leveraging pre-trained convolutional neural networks \(CNNs\), the study fine- tuned models on a dataset of silkworm disease images to achieve high classification accuracy. The approach reduces the need for large labeled datasets specific to silkworms, making it a cost-effective solution for disease detection in sericulture. )
/E (This research explores the application of transfer learning techniques to classify diseases in silkworms. By leveraging pre-trained convolutional neural networks \(CNNs\), the study fine- tuned models on a dataset of silkworm disease images to achieve high classification accuracy. The approach reduces the need for large labeled datasets specific to silkworms, making it a cost-effective solution for disease detection in sericulture. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
