/T (User-Friendly Interface: Designed with a simple and intuitive mobile or web interface to accommodate users with limited technical literacy.Visual cues and minimal text ensure accessibility even in low-literacy regions.  Minimal Technical Expertise Required: Farmers only need to take and upload images of silkworms; the backend AI handles analysis and diagnosis.Step-by-step guidance can be embedded into the app to support first-time users.  Language and Localization Support: The system can be localized in  regional languages, making it more accessible to native sericulture workers.  Quick and Reliable Diagnosis: Real-time feedback allows farmers to act  immediately, improving disease management without delays.Reduces  reliance on manual inspection or waiting for experts.  Integrates with Existing Farming Practices: No change in how farmers  raise silkworms; the system only enhances disease monitoring.Compatible  with current mobile usage habits among rural populations.  Low Infrastructure Dependence: Can function with low-bandwidth )
