1620 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 427 0 R
/T (Overall, Silkworm Disease Detection Using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning bridges a critical technological gap in the sericulture industry by combining AI-driven diagnosis with practical usability for end users. It not only enhances productivity and economic stability for silk farmers but also showcases the potential of AI in agricultural and rural domains. With further enhancements such as edge computing for offline prediction, integration with government agri-portals, and automatic disease trend analysis, Silk Shield can evolve into a comprehensive, intelligent platform for sustainable sericulture management in India and beyond. )
/E (Overall, Silkworm Disease Detection Using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning bridges a critical technological gap in the sericulture industry by combining AI-driven diagnosis with practical usability for end users. It not only enhances productivity and economic stability for silk farmers but also showcases the potential of AI in agricultural and rural domains. With further enhancements such as edge computing for offline prediction, integration with government agri-portals, and automatic disease trend analysis, Silk Shield can evolve into a comprehensive, intelligent platform for sustainable sericulture management in India and beyond. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1621 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 427 0 R
/T (The Silkworm Disease Detection Using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning project successfully demonstrates the application of deep learning techniques, specifically Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\), in the domain of sericulture for early and accurate disease detection in silkworms. By enabling farmers to upload images and receive real-time predictions about potential infections like Pebrine, Grasserie, Flacherie, and Muscardine, the system empowers them to take timely preventive and curative actions. This reduces the risk of widespread outbreaks and promotes healthier silk production. The user-friendly interface, multilingual support, and mobile compatibility ensure that the system is accessible even to farmers in remote and rural areas with limited digital literacy. )
/E (The Silkworm Disease Detection Using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning project successfully demonstrates the application of deep learning techniques, specifically Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\), in the domain of sericulture for early and accurate disease detection in silkworms. By enabling farmers to upload images and receive real-time predictions about potential infections like Pebrine, Grasserie, Flacherie, and Muscardine, the system empowers them to take timely preventive and curative actions. This reduces the risk of widespread outbreaks and promotes healthier silk production. The user-friendly interface, multilingual support, and mobile compatibility ensure that the system is accessible even to farmers in remote and rural areas with limited digital literacy. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
