1629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 428 0 R
/T (The future scope of the Silkworm Disease Detection Using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning system includes enhancing its capabilities through integration with edge computing to enable offline disease detection in remote areas with poor internet connectivity. The model can be further trained on a broader dataset to improve its accuracy across more silkworm breeds and rare diseases. Incorporating real- time weather and environmental data could enable predictive alerts for potential outbreaks. Additionally, integration with IoT-based silkworm rearing environments, government agri- portals, and SMS-based alert systems in local languages would expand its reach and effectiveness, making it a robust decision-support tool for sericulture farmers and agricultural departments. )
/E (The future scope of the Silkworm Disease Detection Using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning system includes enhancing its capabilities through integration with edge computing to enable offline disease detection in remote areas with poor internet connectivity. The model can be further trained on a broader dataset to improve its accuracy across more silkworm breeds and rare diseases. Incorporating real- time weather and environmental data could enable predictive alerts for potential outbreaks. Additionally, integration with IoT-based silkworm rearing environments, government agri- portals, and SMS-based alert systems in local languages would expand its reach and effectiveness, making it a robust decision-support tool for sericulture farmers and agricultural departments. )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
