3761 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Silkworm Disease Detection Using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning project successfully demonstrates the application of deep learning techniques, specifically Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\), in the domain of sericulture for early and accurate disease detection in silkworms. By enabling farmers to upload images and receive real-time predictions about potential infections like Pebrine, Grasserie, Flacherie, and Muscardine, the system empowers them to take timely preventive and curative actions. This reduces the risk of widespread outbreaks and promotes healthier silk production. The user-friendly interface, multilingual support, and mobile compatibility ensure that the system is accessible even to farmers in remote and rural areas with limited digital literacy.)
/Dest [50 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3506 0 R
/Next 3894 0 R
>>
endobj
