/Title (convolutional neural network \(CNN\) model, such as EfficientNet-B3, fine-tuned on a curated dataset of healthy and diseased silkworm images. The model will be trained to detect visual symptoms of common silkworm infections, enabling early and reliable diagnosis.The system will feature a user-friendly mobile and web-based application where farmers can upload images of silkworms taken using their smartphones. Upon uploading, the system will process the image in real time, run it through the trained CNN model, and return the diagnosis along with actionable suggestions or preventive measures. The platform will also include a real-time alert mechanism to notify farmers immediately of potential outbreaks and encourage timely intervention.In addition, the system will maintain  a disease occurrence database for continuous learning and improved accuracy over time. It will be designed to be scalable, allowing integration with future modules like  environmental condition monitoring, pest detection, or multilingual support. Ultimately,  Silk Shield aims to offer a low-cost, accessible, and intelligent tool for improving disease  management in sericulture, especially for small and medium-scale farmers.)
/Dest [36 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4555 0 R
>>
endobj
